\tag{fdip}
\title{Blocking an interaction}
\date{2026-11-28}

\p{A single-site quartic weight changes the Gaussian probabilities
before their block means are taken. How does its exact integral compare
with the polynomial obtained by keeping two coupling orders? The
zero-sum block fluctuation gives a finite Wick calculation; bounds on
an actual potential then control its extracted quartic coefficient.}

